{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RP-01 truncation clarification and correction to the preceding cache note. Current Rebar has three distinct behaviors: (1) source ticket/system/user/tool input is not truncated at this seam; plan review context overflow keeps full content, splits criteria/escalates model windows, then emits a decomposition failure rather than chunking content; (2) a provider response with finish_reason length/max_tokens/refusal/content_filter is rejected before repair as UnretryableOutputError and never accepted as a verdict; (3) only a failed intermediate response copied into a retry prompt is capped at 2,000 characters. The original failed response is parsed in full, accepted output is returned in full, and the optional final-failure artifact stores the complete final reply. Proposed same-run finding: Pydantic ProcessHistory is unsuitable because _agent_graph commits processed messages back into state. Offline probe: a 5,000-character failed response became 2,013 both on the retry wire and in result.all_messages(). A documented model_request wrapper is non-destructive: the provider still saw the same 2,013-character projection and 2,211-character retry request, while result.all_messages() retained all 5,000 characters. Live Anthropic and Bedrock reruns with this wrapper reproduced the prior cache counts exactly: agentic retry read/write 3,920/289, and stored assistant lengths included the full 5,000. Revised constraint: never truncate source inputs, tool evidence, accepted output, or stored raw responses; check provider truncation before repair and fail closed. Remaining maintainer choice: retain the existing 2,000-character retry-only projection through model_request, or intentionally remove it and send the full failed intermediate response back. Research note and recovery report updated; no production code changed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786910881278914001,"uuid":"6e9e9f70-d850-4d01-a2cb-09df9238ece9"}